framework PurposeBusV1ReleasePreparation:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain PurposeBus:
  description "Local-first coordination queue and Skill-only Codex Plugin"

problem P1:
  |
    What exact local source, compatibility freeze, clean-room evidence, and
    rollback package satisfy T_V1_RELEASE_PREP without publishing, installing
    into an active profile, or starting T_PUBLISH_V1_0_0?

premise PR1:
  |
    The owner instructed the next PERT task to proceed. T_V1_RELEASE_PREP
    explicitly requires a 1.0.0 core source, a compatible Codex Plugin
    candidate, final clean-room acceptance, migration and rollback evidence,
    supported-surface and install or uninstall documentation, a changelog,
    release artifacts, and exact revisions without publication.

premise PR2:
  |
    Proceeding with release preparation does not authorize commit, push,
    publication, release, deployment, public Plugin Directory submission,
    active-profile installation, Connector use, or live PurposeBus mutation.

premise PR3:
  |
    The accepted RC and Plugin package are immutable predecessor evidence.
    Release preparation must reference their exact digests and artifacts rather
    than rewrite their contracts or report their old versions as the new source.

evidence EV1:
  |
    PERT digest 99cd699472ca835c73a698e4b04a59235c468c47a9bdcaf2d1d20293482cb545
    reports only T_V1_RELEASE_PREP as ready and recommended. The following
    publication task remains gated on a separate explicit authorization.

evidence EV2:
  |
    Local HEAD and the independently read GitHub feature/local-mvp ref both
    equal 2a2b3a68c8f44a4107268e4fd51949106a37d486. Existing accepted beta, RC,
    and Plugin work is uncommitted in the current mixed worktree and must be
    preserved.

evidence EV3:
  |
    Current core package metadata and purposebus.__version__ both report
    0.2.0a1. The current Plugin package is
    1.0.0+codex.20260908092104 but its Skill and machine contract require core
    ==0.2.0a1. The read-only MCP adapter also rejects every core version other
    than 0.2.0a1.

evidence EV4:
  |
    The accepted RC source archive, core 0.2.0a1 wheel, evidence manifest, and
    the accepted Plugin 1.0 package archive exist under content-addressed local
    build paths with the digests recorded by their predecessor contracts and
    owner-facing evidence.

evidence EV5:
  |
    State schema remains 1 and current tests prove supported state reopens
    without migration or mutation. The RC verifier already exercises isolated
    core upgrade, rollback and re-upgrade, corrupt-state fail-closed recovery,
    bounded load, reproducible wheels, and temporary-profile Plugin transition.

evidence EV6:
  |
    Current official OpenAI Plugin documentation requires plugin.json, permits
    a Skill-only Plugin, separates local marketplace testing from public
    publication, and requires testing the complete changed Plugin in a new
    conversation with direct, indirect, follow-up, negative, and boundary
    prompts. The plugin-creator workflow requires a new cachebuster whenever
    existing Plugin source changes.

premise IN1:
  |
    Inference: the phrase 1.0.0 core source is a material release identity, not
    a label for the already accepted 0.2.0a1 RC. A Plugin-only bundle would not
    meet the explicit completion contract. Therefore both project metadata
    version sources must become 1.0.0 and every exact compatible consumer must
    be tested and pinned to that version.

premise IN2:
  |
    Inference: no storage migration implementation is required because the new
    core preserves state schema 1 and behavior. The required migration result
    is an observed no-migration transition from the accepted 0.2.0a1 state to
    1.0.0, followed by rollback and re-upgrade against the same isolated state.

premise ALT1:
  |
    Alternative: leave core at 0.2.0a1 and call the Plugin 1.0 archive the
    release package. This is rejected because it omits the requested 1.0.0 core
    and leaves release metadata contradictory.

premise ALT2:
  |
    Alternative: widen Plugin or MCP compatibility to a range. This is rejected
    because only one exact replacement core will be tested by this preparation;
    a wider range would claim unobserved compatibility.

premise ALT3:
  |
    Alternative: replace historical RC and Plugin contracts with current
    hashes. This is rejected because it destroys predecessor provenance and
    makes rollback evidence circular.

pending PD1:
  |
    Windows or Desktop GUI behavior, other operating systems or architectures,
    public directory review, signing, destination permissions, server-side
    revisions, and clean installation from a public index remain unverified and
    outside local release preparation.

pending PD2:
  |
    A local source snapshot is not a Git revision. Until a separately authorized
    commit exists, the release contract can record the current base HEAD plus
    immutable content digests, but it must not claim a candidate commit SHA or a
    server-side release ref.

decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, PR2, PR3, EV1, EV2, EV3, EV4, EV5, EV6, IN1, IN2, ALT1, ALT2, ALT3, PD1, PD2:
  |
    Start T_V1_RELEASE_PREP in the existing worktree. Change the core package
    and runtime version to exactly 1.0.0. Update the Skill-only Plugin and the
    read-only MCP adapter to require exactly core 1.0.0, then use the
    plugin-creator cachebuster helper once so the changed Plugin has a new exact
    local identity. Preserve the accepted RC and Plugin contracts as historical
    predecessors. Add an additive machine-readable v1 release contract, a
    changelog, a release-preparation runbook, contract tests, and a one-command
    clean-room verifier. Bind critical source hashes, public schemas, state
    schema, package identities, predecessor artifact digests, supported and
    unsupported surfaces, destinations still requiring authorization, and
    excluded authority. Build the core, MCP, and controller wheels twice from a
    normalized source snapshot; assemble deterministic core and Plugin release
    artifacts; verify 0.2.0a1 to 1.0.0 state reopen without migration, rollback,
    re-upgrade, corruption behavior, bounded load, isolated Plugin install,
    upgrade, rollback, uninstall, and raw CLI fallback. Re-run the changed exact
    Plugin in isolated fresh Codex sessions for direct, indirect, follow-up,
    negative, and cross-host boundary behavior, and retain exact limitations.
    Run all repository and integration checks. If a material clean-room or
    fresh-session check cannot be completed, leave the task in progress and
    report the blocker. Otherwise record content digests and base HEAD, finish
    T_V1_RELEASE_PREP, and stop before the separate authorization gate. Do not
    commit, push, publish, release, deploy, mutate an active profile, add Plugin
    MCP or app components, use a Connector, or start T_PUBLISH_V1_0_0.

query Q1:
  .document.steps[].statement | select(.role == "decision" and len(.based_on) > 0)
